# Newline between identifier and dot: dot is always emitted as Dot token.
# a.b (no gap) = dot access; a\n.b = call a (head) then Dot+b (parser may error or handle unexpectedly)
# With bracket access removed, a[0] and a [0] are identical: both parse as a call to a with dict arg [0].
[a [0]]
=== out
[a [0]]
